@TITLE@ iOS kit (iPadOS and iOS, arm64 devices, iOS 16 or newer)
=================================================================

What the Mac app's "Play on iPad" builds the game's iPad (or iPhone) app
from. $kit below is this folder (Contents/Resources/ios-kit). The app's own
copy is read-only (sealed with the app): build in a folder of your own.

What's here
-----------
lib/lib@GAME@_ios_kit.a  Everything but the lifted code, one static archive
                         for arm64 devices (iphoneos SDK): the game's
                         library and runtime, SDL3, Dear ImGui, volk,
                         libchdr (with LZMA, miniz, zstd's decompressor,
                         dr_flac) and MoltenVK (its release's static
                         library, App Store build: no private API).
include/                 The runtime's headers, which the lifted code
                         includes (as the desktop kit's include/).
build-flags.txt          `name = value` lines, $kit this folder:
                           sdk = iphoneos
                           cxxflags = what each lifted .cpp is compiled with
                         There is no native line: the code runs on every
                         arm64 iPad and iPhone with iOS 16 or newer.
xcode/                   The app's Xcode project: QilinGame.xcodeproj
                         (scheme QilinGame), Info.plist, Game.xcconfig (this
                         game's defaults), QilinGame.xcconfig (the build
                         settings), app.c, Assets.xcassets (the icon).
VERSION                  The release this kit is from.

Building and installing
-----------------------
1. Compile each lifted .cpp (qilin lift's output, as for the Mac):
     xcrun --sdk iphoneos clang++ <cxxflags, $kit replaced> -c <file>.cpp -o <file>.o
2. Put them in one static library:
     xcrun --sdk iphoneos libtool -static -o <work>/liblifted.a <the .o files>
3. Copy $kit/xcode to a folder you can write to, <work>/xcode, and build:
     xcodebuild -project <work>/xcode/QilinGame.xcodeproj -scheme QilinGame \
       -configuration Release -destination generic/platform=iOS \
       -derivedDataPath <work>/derived -allowProvisioningUpdates \
       DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=<the player's team ID> \
       PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER=<an identifier made once per player> \
       PRODUCT_NAME=@EXE@ \
       QILIN_LIFTED_LIB=<work>/liblifted.a \
       QILIN_KIT_LIB=$kit/lib/lib@GAME@_ios_kit.a \
       build
   The app is <work>/derived/Build/Products/Release-iphoneos/@EXE@.app
   (PRODUCT_NAME.app). `archive` works too (-archivePath <path>), but
   `build` is enough for a development install. Paths may have spaces.
   Optional settings: QILIN_DISPLAY_NAME (the name under the icon and in
   the Files app; default "@TITLE@"), MARKETING_VERSION and
   CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION (default this kit's version).
4. Install it: xcrun devicectl device install app --device <device> <the .app>
5. Copy the player's disc image into the app's Documents folder (devicectl
   device copy to, the app's data container, destination Documents/): one
   image only, a .chd (one file), or a .cue with its .bin tracks, or a .gdi
   with its tracks, all side by side. With none, or more than one, the game
   says so and waits ("Check again"). The player can also copy it with the
   Files app: On My iPad, @TITLE@.

On the iPad
-----------
Documents/qilin/@GAME@ is the game's data folder (settings, the memory card,
the saves' history, texture packs) and log.txt, the log of the last start
(the launch environment's QILIN_LOG=console keeps it on stderr instead).
The game is played with a controller (MFi, Xbox, PlayStation); Back and
Start together (or Esc on a keyboard) open the settings. It pauses when the
app goes to the background.
